ories there are some very good stories  set on modern day earth in doctor who in  the modern era but  it is by default kind of the most boring  place to set a story and you have to do  a bunch of other stuff to make it  interesting which sometimes the show  does but you're starting at a  disadvantage doing that and lastly this  one is probably more subjective than any  of these and like again if you enjoy any  of the aspects that i liked and missed  them when he was gone or liked that they  were continued when he was gone that's  fine this is ultimately my opinion  and this last one is uh the most sort of  my opinion than the others and probably  the one i'm most likely to get called  out on but i'm gonna bring it up anyway  he was kind of self-indulgent  and again that's not to say that other  creators weren't moffett  could get very self-indulgent but uh the  way that they would do it is kind of  reflective of their approach where  moffat would get self-indulgent by  basically  disappearing up his own  big brain  and trying to be super ultra clever  rtd would get self-indulgent in a bit of  a more traditional way and i think you  can look to the finales for that  in hindsight series one probably has the  most restrained finale  and that ends with the companion having  the power of a god bringing back uh jack  hardness and apparently at the time  wiping out all daleks including the  dalek emperor and then the doctor dying  like that's big and that's the most  restrained that it gets we get to series  two and we have the very  uh honestly fan fakie idea of daleks and  cybermen just  going at it and again like none of these  are bad ideas but i'm going over the  pattern with you then we get to series  three  we bring back the master  and we have this whole we just we  literally turned the doctrine to jesus i  mean not literally literally but  practically i forgive you  he is reborn through the power of belief  in him it's  really kind of self-indulgent in terms  of the character and then series four  and then ultimately the end of time part  two gets really self-indulgent on the  show as a whole in terms of well we  gotta bring everybody in that we  possibly can and we gotta have the  doctor go on this massive goodbye tour  stopping in on every companion that we  can get to come in for a day of shooting  and  again i get it it's kind of the return  of the king thing where this has been  going on so long if we're ending this  story or in the case of doctor who  ending the show runner and this doctor's  eras then yeah  we kind of earned the right to  have these extra things but again the  indulgence  escalated during his time  at times honestly to the detriment of  the story while there is  a superficial thrill at things like  daleks versus cybermen and so many uh  past characters coming back in journey's  end and then having the doctor stop by  and say goodbye to all these people  there is a little bit of a thrill to  that as strictly as a narrative function  it  drags it bloats  and that  as i said kind of got  worse as time went on  now  that's all i really have in terms of  broad things because what i didn't want  this to do was to pick out specific  episodes that he wrote and just go  through a whole list of nitpicks cause  you know what you can watch my uh  overdue doctor who reviews uh i'll try  and put a playlist up there if you want  to see me take those on one episode at a  time and bring up whatever my issues are  that's not what i wanted here i wanted  to talk about the broad strokes and the  repeated things that he did across his  arrow that  i didn't love  does it mean i don't like rtd no no it  doesn't doesn't mean i'm not excited for  him to come back no it absolutely does  not  but  i said i had issues nothing you asked  there you go  so  what do you think about my assessment  here uh even if you think i'm very wrong  please be polite about it but whatever  your thoughts are drop something down  the comments let's talk about it like  share and subscribe all the usual stuff  i got a patreon that is how i pay the  bills and i'm able to  talk to you folks on a regular basis so  maybe consider supporting me there  there's also youtube memberships if you  want to go that way but don't worry too  much about it  because uh at the end of the day  you are the council i'm just running the  meetings and until next time this  council  is adjourned  [Music]  this video wouldn't have been possible  without the support of my patrons and i  want to give special thanks to jared  boyce  mj the doctor tracy scrabbit vincent  paul bartolucci kailyn schwartz edelman  robin moore ross schultz and shayla  gorla  thanks so much  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  now  [Music]  foreign  [Music]
 

